// A clef change at a multi-measure-rest run's LEFT bound. Two LilyPond behaviours meet
// here, and this is the pair to test/mmr-key-change-bound — a clef differs from a key or
// time change in WHERE IT IS DRAWN, while grouping the same way:
//
//  1. RUN GROUPING — identical to key/time. The change does NOT break the bar out of the
//     run: LilyPond hangs it on the run's opening NonMusicalPaperColumn, so
//     `\clef bass R1*5` stays ONE 5-bar church rest. Lily# used to eject the bar and
//     print an individual whole rest plus a 4-bar church rest.
//
//  2. DRAWING — a clef is engraved BEFORE the bar line, where a key or time change goes
//     after it. LilyPond's unbroken break-align order is `clef, cue-clef, staff-bar,
//     key-cancellation, key-signature, time-signature`, so the clef's right edge sits
//     Clef.space-alist (staff-bar . (extra-space . 0.7)) = 0.700 left of the bar line.
//     Its width is charged to the PRECEDING measure's closing gap, not to the run.
//
// Consequence, and the reason this fixture is worth its snapshot: the run itself does not
// get wider. Verified on LilyPond 2.24.4 — bar line to bar line across `R1*5` is
// 14.133856 both with and without the leading clef. Only the paper column's ORIGIN moves.
//
// LILYPOND-REF: scm/define-grobs.scm:650-664 BreakAlignment.break-align-orders (unbroken),
// :291-302 BarLine.space-alist, :914-925 Clef.space-alist,
// lily/multi-measure-rest-engraver.cc process_music, lily/note-spacing.cc:77-108.
title "MMR run with a clef change at its bound"
composer "Lily#"

tempo 120
time 4/4
key c major

part melody

section Main {
  melody {
    c4 d e f |
    clef bass R1*5 |
    g4 a b c |
  }
}

form main { Main }

score main "mmr-clef-change-bound" {
  staff melody
}
